# Fixed 2026-10-11, defect 608, lane b20-check: the shape beside it whose
# value is `()`. Before the repair the line was told `bound_unit`; now it is
# told once as a cell nothing re-binds, the resolver's message, which the
# checker's waits behind as it does for every line. Its certain fix writes
# `_ = g(1)`, which `check` then refuses as `bound_unit`, so this case
# carries an `.applied` and no `.fixed`.

function g(x: i64)
    print(x)

function main()
    _ = g(1)  #~ never_rebound
    print("done")
